{"availability":"available","full":"Xiangyu-Hu/SPHinXsys","name":"SPHinXsys","description":"SPHinXsys provides C++ APIs for engineering simulation and optimization. It aims at complex systems driven by fluid, structure, multi-body dynamics and beyond. The multi-physics library is based on a unique and unified computational framework by which strong coupling has been achieved for all involved physics.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C++","stars":597,"forks":389,"created":"2019-05-28T17:05:34Z","updated":"2026-10-06T12:51:21Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://xiangyu-hu.github.io/SPHinXsys/","topics":["computer-aided-engineering","cpp","finite-volume-method","fluid-dynamics","fluid-structure-interaction","gpu","hacktoberfest","high-performance-computing","multi-physics","multiphysics-coupling","smoothed-particle-hydrodynamics","solid-dynamics","sycl"],"demo":"https://xiangyu-hu.github.io/SPHinXsys/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.750Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.750Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.750Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.750Z","stars":597,"forks":389}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SPHinXsys (pronunciation: s'fink-sis) is an acronym from Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics for industrial compleX systems. The multi-physics library uses SPH (smoothed particle hydrodynamics) as the underlying numerical method for both particle-based and mesh-based discretization. Due to the unified computational framework, SPHinXsys is able to carry out simulation and optimization at the same time. For more information on the SPHinXsys project, please check the project website: .","You are also welcomed to check SPHinXsim, which is an multi-physics simulator based on SPHinXsys with interactive visualization and particle generation. SPHinXsim provides independent C++, Python and large language model (LLM) user interfaces."],"features":